# Composed kaish primer at every context create — the per-context half of
# adopting kaish-help (docs/composable-help.md step 4: "kaijutsu/kaibo adopt
# kaish-help"). `kj kaish primer` composes the model + operating contract +
# builtins straight from the linked kaish-help crate
# (crates/kaijutsu-kernel/src/kj/kaish.rs) — nothing here is hand-copied
# prose, so a kaish release reaches every newly-created context without a
# kaijutsu edit.
#
# No static copy is stored to rot: this recomposes fresh on every
# `create` and lands as an ordinary Role::System/BlockKind::Text block (folds
# into the cached system prompt like S00-stance.kai — see that script's
# comment for why S25-datetime.kai deliberately does NOT do this).
primer="$(kj kaish primer)"

# Fail loudly on an empty primer instead of seeding an empty system block.
# `$(...)` swallows a failing command's exit status into an empty capture, so
# without this guard a broken `kj kaish primer` produced a zero-length
# Role::System block, the script still exited 0, and the rc lifecycle recorded
# an ordinary Trace — a context silently missing its kaish guidance with
# nothing anywhere saying so. Exiting non-zero makes the lifecycle write an
# Error block instead (kj/lifecycle.rs), which is the whole point of the
# create lifecycle being observable.
test -n "$primer" || exit 1

kj block create --role system --kind text --content "$primer"
